    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3193": {
      "title": "YourPace Academic Success Coach",
      "description": "YourPace Academic Success Coach - UMS Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs YourPace Academic Success Coach Presque Isle, ME, United States (Remote) Job Info Job Identification 3193 Job Category Academic Student Services Posting Date 09/23/2026, 12:58 PM Locations 181 Main Street, Presque Isle, ME, 04769, US (Remote) Apply Before 09/30/2026, 02:00 PM Business Unit University of Maine at Presque Isle Job Schedule Full time Regular or Temporary Regular Department UMPI CBE Adult Learner Bargaining Unit Universities of Maine Professional Staff Association (UMPSA) Job Description The University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) is seeking to hire a YourPace Academic Success Coach . The YourPace Academic Success Coach will serve as the primary point of contact for students from the point of matriculation through graduation, providing seamless, student-centered support across the entire enrollment and academic journey. This role combines proactive outreach, degree planning, and academic coaching to promote student persistence, retention, and success particularly during the early stages of the student experience. The Coach supports students in navigating University policies and systems, connects them to resources, and helps them develop the skills and confidence necessary for success in the YourPace learning model. Working collaboratively with faculty, staff, and administrators across departments, the Coach ensures that each student receives timely, accurate, and personalized guidance. Work is conducted in a collaborative environment, with remote, hybrid, or in-person work options determined in consultation with the successful candidate. Occasional travel to campus may be required for training or events. The standard schedule is Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. EST and will require some nights and weekends. For a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications, please review the full job description here . The salary for this full time job is $47,112.33. The university will take into consideration the salary of current UMS employees for transfer/promotion depending on skills and experience. Additional benefits include medical, retirement, dental, vision, and tuition waiver programs for employees and dependents.  The UMS is a recipient of the Wellness Councils of America’s Well Workplace Award and offers wellness programs. Visit our benefits website to learn more. Required Qualifications, Knowledge, and Skills: Bachelor’s degree and 3–5 years of experience in a professional setting, such as advising, counseling, admissions, tutoring, education, or customer service. Exceptional interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to build rapport and motivate students. Proven organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage multiple priorities. Ability to interpret and explain academic policies and degree requirements. Experience with Microsoft Office Suite, Google Workspace, and communication technologies (e.g., Zoom). Commitment to maintaining confidentiality and FERPA compliance. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced, student-centered environment. Strong problem-solving skills and a proactive approach to addressing student needs. For remote/hybrid work: reliable high-speed internet (minimum 25 Mbps) and a dedicated, private workspace that meets confidentiality requirements. Preferred Qualifications Master’s Degree. Five or more years of experience in higher education or student success roles. Experience working with adult learners or competency-based education models. Familiarity with University of Maine System technologies, including MaineStreet and BrightSpace. How to apply Materials must be submitted via “Apply Now\" below or visit the UMPI Careers Page . For application to be considered complete you must create an applicant profile (application) and submit ALL of the following: Cover letter Resume Important Information About the Recruitment Process: Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis. For full consideration, applications must be received by 5:00 p.m. EST on September 30, 2026. Applications received after this date may be considered at the discretion of the University. Finalist candidates will be asked to provide a list of professional references. A background check will be conducted for the selected candidate. Please note: The University is unable to consider applicants who require visa sponsorship. About the University For more than a century, the University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) has helped students build successful professional careers. UMPI offers life-changing opportunities in a caring, small-university environment for 3,000 traditional and non-traditional students from Maine, across the United States, and around the world. To learn more, visit the University of Maine at Presque Isle website . Situated on 150 acres amidst the rolling hills and potato fields of northern Maine, UMPI strives to be the region’s premier learning institution while helping to stimulate cultural and economic development throughout Aroostook County and the State of Maine. Serving as an educational and cultural center for the area, university facilities host lectures, academic programs, concerts, dance performances, art exhibits, and plays that benefit the entire region. You can also explore community resources and regional attractions by reading more about what Aroostook County has to offer . Equal Opportunity Statement -The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act - The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report. If you have any questions, contact Safety and Security 111 Campus Center 181 Main St., Presque Isle, ME 04769 Phone: (207) 768-9580. About Us About the University of Maine System The University of Maine System (UMS), established in 1968, consists of seven universities and the University of Maine School of Law, spread across various locations in Maine. UMS provides system-wide services and governance from these locations, leveraging the distinct strengths and collaborations among its institutions to advance strategic priorities for UMS and the state of Maine. Choosing UMS means opting for a high quality of life supported by excellent benefits such as tuition waivers, robust retirement contributions, and comprehensive insurance coverage including medical, dental, vision, life, and disability. Maine's diverse landscapes, from accessible wilderness and rugged coastline to urban centers and rural communities, offer numerous cultural activities, strong public schools, safe neighborhoods, and high-quality healthcare. Discover more about Maine's exemplary lifestyle on the Maine Office of Tourism website . Apply Now Accreditation Privacy Policy Freedom of Information Act Accessibility Title IX © 2026 University of Maine System University Students Faculty & Staff Trustees Data & Policy I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page YourPace Academic Success Coach - UMS Careers loaded"
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3192": {
      "title": "Director of Campus Technology",
      "description": "Director of Campus Technology - UMS Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Director of Campus Technology Presque Isle, ME, United States (On-site) Job Info Job Identification 3192 Job Category Information Technology [Sa1] Posting Date 09/23/2026, 09:05 AM Locations 181 Main Street, Presque Isle, ME, 04769, US (On-site) Business Unit Governance and University Services Grade Professional Salaried grade 06 Job Schedule Full time Regular or Temporary Regular Department GUS Campus Services - UMPI Bargaining Unit Universities of Maine Professional Staff Association (UMPSA) Workdays Monday to Friday Job Description The University of Maine System is seeking a Director of Campus Technology to provide strategic and operational leadership for technology services at the University of Maine at Presque Isle. This position serves as the primary connection between campus leadership and UMS IT, translating campus goals into practical technology strategies, services, and resources. The Director will lead campus technology initiatives, oversee campus-based IT staff, strengthen service delivery, and coordinate the campus response to significant technical incidents and disruptions. The successful candidate will be a collaborative leader who can build trusted relationships, balance competing priorities, and connect the distinct needs of the campus with System wide IT strategy and capabilities. This is an office-based position that may require travel to other University locations or work sites. The Director may occasionally work evenings and weekends to support campus events, significant service disruptions, and other campus needs. What You Will Do Build and sustain strong relationships with campus leadership, faculty, staff, students, and UMS IT partners to promote strategic alignment and responsive technology services. Consult with campus leaders and administrative personnel to identify current and emerging technology needs, evaluate options, recommend improvements, and coordinate solutions. Oversee academic, administrative, and research related technology services at the assigned campus and promote consistent, efficient, customer focused service delivery. Lead, coach, and support campus IT staff, including performance management, employee development, training, and appropriate corrective or disciplinary processes. Manage stakeholder expectations, identify gaps between campus needs and available IT capabilities, and collaborate across UMS IT to develop effective solutions. Provide campus and IT leadership with executive level reports and key performance indicators related to Tier 2 support and customer service. Coordinate campus response to significant technical incidents and service disruptions, including communication with campus and System stakeholders. Participate in UMS IT leadership activities, campus committees, and the UMS IT Service Desk Council to advance shared priorities and service improvements. Develop budget requests, monitor designated technology budgets, and represent UMS IT with relevant external groups, partners, and service providers. Maintain compliance with University and UMS IT standards, policies, and procedures while remaining current on technology solutions and service management practices. What We Are Looking For Required Qualifications A bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education and professional experience, including leadership or supervisory responsibility. Seven years of progressively responsible experience in mid-to-senior level information technology roles. Broad knowledge of enterprise technology environments, including networking, data communications, telecommunications, hardware, and software systems. Demonstrated ability to lead and develop employees and guide teams toward organizational goals. Strong organizational and project management skills, including the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Excellent written, verbal, presentation, negotiation, and conflict management skills, including the ability to explain complex information to varied audiences. A collaborative and transparent leadership approach, strong customer service orientation, and the ability to work effectively with people from diverse backgrounds and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications Experience providing technology leadership and services in higher education, including support for faculty, researchers, staff, and students. Experience working effectively in a complex, decentralized organization. Advanced knowledge of enterprise infrastructure, endpoint technologies, networking, telecommunications, and IT service delivery. Experience developing and implementing technology roadmaps and leading initiatives across multiple teams and functional areas. What We Offer: Our comprehensive benefits package can be worth up to 50% of your annual salary and is designed to support your health, financial well-being, professional growth, and work-life balance. Benefits include: Competitive salary: $65,000–$75,000 commensurate with education and experience. This is a fixed range set within a predefined wage band, so we're not able to negotiate a starting salary above it. Comprehensive health benefits , including medical, dental, vision, flexible spending accounts (FSA), and Health Savings Account (HSA) options. Employer-paid benefits , including basic life insurance and long-term disability coverage, with additional voluntary coverage options available. Retirement plan through TIAA with a 10% employer contribution and opportunities for additional tax-deferred retirement savings. Generous paid time off , including vacation and sick leave, plus 13 paid holidays each year. Tuition waiver program for employees, including graduate courses and Maine Law, plus substantial tuition discounts for eligible spouses and dependent children. Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and wellness programs supporting your health and well-being. Professional development and opportunities to grow your career within Maine's public universities. Additional voluntary benefits, including pet insurance, home and auto insurance discounts, and supplemental disability and life insurance options Apply Today! Materials must be submitted via “Apply Now” below. You will need to complete an application and upload the following materials: A cover letter that describes your experience, interests, and suitability for the position. A resume/curriculum vitae. Important items to know about the recruitment process: Review of applications will begin immediately. The position will remain open until filled. Incomplete application materials cannot be considered. Candidates selected to proceed to the final stages of the search process will be requested to provide three (3) names and contact information for references. The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screenings. ⚠️ Work authorization: This position requires U.S. work authorization that does not require employer sponsorship now or in the future. We are unable to consider applicants who require visa sponsorship or OPT extensions at any point. EEO Statement The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/. Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish, and distribute an Annual Security Report (ASR), and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. View the University’s Annual Security Report (PDF) . If you wish to have a paper copy of the ASR or need to have a copy of the ASR in an accessible format, the University will provide such a copy upon request. Please contact Safety and Security, University of Maine at Presque, 111 Campus Center, 181 Main St., Presque Isle, ME 04769, 207.768.9580. About Us About the University of Maine System The University of Maine System (UMS), established in 1968, consists of seven universities and the University of Maine School of Law, spread across various locations in Maine. UMS provides system-wide services and governance from these locations, leveraging the distinct strengths and collaborations among its institutions to advance strategic priorities for UMS and the state of Maine. Choosing UMS means opting for a high quality of life supported by excellent benefits such as tuition waivers, robust retirement contributions, and comprehensive insurance coverage including medical, dental, vision, life, and disability. Maine's diverse landscapes, from accessible wilderness and rugged coastline to urban centers and rural communities, offer numerous cultural activities, strong public schools, safe neighborhoods, and high-quality healthcare. Discover more about Maine's exemplary lifestyle on the Maine Office of Tourism website . Apply Now Accreditation Privacy Policy Freedom of Information Act Accessibility Title IX © 2026 University of Maine System University Students Faculty & Staff Trustees Data & Policy I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Director of Campus Technology - UMS Careers loaded"
