ravel, contests, awards, recruitment, fundraising, and budget matters. Transport student athletes to and from games as needed. Report scores, statistics, injuries, and other required information accurately and promptly. Coordinate publicity efforts with the Athletics office. Ensure compliance with applicable safety protocols and University and departmental policies. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or equivalent experience Demonstrated experience coaching women's lacrosse. Ability to recruit, organize, instruct, and supervise student athletes. Ability to create a positive and educational athletic experience. Valid driver's license in good standing. Preferred Qualifications: Experience coaching at the collegiate level. Experience supporting the personal growth and development of student athletes. Experience promoting and supporting student athlete academic success. Why UMA? At UMA, we're dedicated to transforming the lives of students across Maine and beyond through high-quality distance and onsite education, excellence in student support. UMA is the third-largest public university in Maine. In addition to its main campus in the state's capital, UMA also serves students in Bangor (UMA Bangor) and through UMA Centers around the state. We provide opportunities at  multiple locations and online, making us a top choice for students of all ages. Application Process To be considered for this position you will need to \"Apply\" and upload the following documentation: A cover letter fully describing your qualifications and experiences with specific reference to the required and preferred qualifications. A resume Candidates select to proceed to the final stages of the search process will be requested to provide a list of references. Review of applications will begin immediately. This position will stay open until filled. Materials received after September 27, 2026, will be reviewed at the discretion of the University. Incomplete application materials will not be con