    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3122": {
      "title": "Technical Coordinator",
      "description": "Technical Coordinator - UMS Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Technical Coordinator Portland, ME, United States (On-site) Job Info Job Identification 3122 Job Category Information Technology [Sa1] Posting Date 09/02/2026, 01:27 PM Locations P.O. Box 9300, Portland, ME, 04104, US (On-site) Business Unit Governance and University Services Grade Professional Salaried grade 03 Job Schedule Full time Regular or Temporary Regular Department GUS Campus Services - USM Bargaining Unit Universities of Maine Professional Staff Association (UMPSA) Workdays Monday to Friday Job Description The University of Maine System is looking for a Technical Coordinator to join our Campus Card & Cellular Services IT team. In this role, you'll provide specialized technical and operational support for the systems and technologies that support Campus Card & Cellular Services across the University of Maine System (UMS). You'll work with applications, databases, access control technologies, specialized hardware, and cellular devices while collaborating with UMS IT teams, campus partners, and vendors. This is a great opportunity for someone who enjoys troubleshooting, learning new technologies, working across different technical areas, and helping turn technical solutions into reliable services for users across the University. This full-time role is located on the University of Southern Maine's Portland campus with a work schedule of Monday through Friday from 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM, with occasional nights and weekends if needed. What You'll Do Support and troubleshoot Campus Card applications, databases, hardware, access control technologies, and related systems. Create and maintain reports, database queries, scripts, and data validation processes that support operations and data integrity. Coordinate and support hardware and software installations, testing, upgrades, and technology deployments. Monitor recurring technical processes and help identify and resolve system and operational issues. Provide technical assistance, consultation, and training to Card Services staff, campus partners, and other users. Support the planning, testing, and implementation of new services, applications, and system enhancements. Develop technical documentation, procedures, user guides, and training resources. Support Card Office technologies and operations, including card production systems, access permissions, and offline lock technologies. Coordinate assigned technical projects and collaborate with UMS IT colleagues, campuses, and vendors to support effective service delivery. Supervise and provide technical guidance to student employees. What We're Looking For A bachelor's degree in information technology, computer science, information systems, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience supporting software applications, computer hardware, operating systems, databases, or related technologies. Experience troubleshooting technical issues in a customer-focused environment. Experience working with reports, database queries, scripts, or similar tools supporting technical operations and data integrity. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills and an interest in learning new technologies. Strong communication, organizational, interpersonal, and customer service skills. The ability to manage multiple priorities and work independently while collaborating effectively with technical colleagues and campus partners. Preferred Qualifications Experience with one or more of the following: Campus Card, identity, access control, transaction, or similar technologies. Campus Card platforms such as Transact, Best BASIS, Instant ID, or comparable systems. Technology services in a higher education environment. Web content management platforms such as WordPress or Liferay. Technology implementations, technical documentation, or technology training. Relevant information technology certifications. Please review the full Technical Coordinator job description for more information. What We Offer: Our comprehensive benefits package can be worth up to 50% of your annual salary and is designed to support your health, financial well-being, professional growth, and work-life balance. Benefits include: Competitive salary: $52,000 - $57,000 commensurate with education and experience. This is a fixed range set within a predefined wage band, se we are not able to negotiate a starting salary above this range. Comprehensive health benefits, including medical, dental, vision, flexible spending account (FSA), and Health Savings Account (HSA) options. Employer-paid benefits , including basic life insurance and long-term disability coverage, with additional voluntary coverage options available. Retirement plan through TIAA with 10% employer contribution and opportunities for additional tax-deferred retirement savings. Generous paid time off, including vacation and sick leave, plus 13 paid holidays each year. Tuition waiver program for employees, including graduate courses and Maine Law, plus substantial tuition discounts for eligible spouses and dependent children. Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and wellness programs supporting your health and well-being. Professional Development and opportunities to grow your career within Maine's public university system. Additional voluntary benefits, including pet insurance, home and auto insurance discounts, and supplemental disability and life insurance options. Why Join the University of Maine System? The University of Maine System provides an opportunity to work in a collaborative technology environment supporting Maine's public universities. In this role, you'll work with colleagues and campus partners across the System while developing expertise in technologies that support essential campus services. If you enjoy solving technical problems, learning new systems, and working with a variety of people and technologies, we encourage you to apply. Apply Today! Materials must be submitted via \"Apply Now\" below. You will need to complete an application and upload the following: A cover letter that describes your experience, interests, and suitability for the position. A resume/curriculum. Important items to know about the recruitment process: Review of applications will begin immediately. The position will remain open until filled. For full consideration, applications need to be submitted by September 13, 2026. Incomplete application materials cannot be considered. Candidates selected to proceed to the final stages of the search process will be requested to provide three (3) names and contact information for references. The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screenings. ⚠️ Work authorization: This position requires U.S. work authorization that does not require employer sponsorship now or in the future. We are unable to consider applicants who require visa sponsorship or OPT extensions at any point. EEO Statement The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/. About Us About the University of Maine System The University of Maine System (UMS), established in 1968, consists of seven universities and the University of Maine School of Law, spread across various locations in Maine. UMS provides system-wide services and governance from these locations, leveraging the distinct strengths and collaborations among its institutions to advance strategic priorities for UMS and the state of Maine. Choosing UMS means opting for a high quality of life supported by excellent benefits such as tuition waivers, robust retirement contributions, and comprehensive insurance coverage including medical, dental, vision, life, and disability. Maine's diverse landscapes, from accessible wilderness and rugged coastline to urban centers and rural communities, offer numerous cultural activities, strong public schools, safe neighborhoods, and high-quality healthcare. Discover more about Maine's exemplary lifestyle on the Maine Office of Tourism website . Apply Now Accreditation Privacy Policy Freedom of Information Act Accessibility Title IX © 2026 University of Maine System University Students Faculty & Staff Trustees Data & Policy I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Technical Coordinator - UMS Careers loaded"
